// RC44 Targets data — built from local B&G H5000 CSV telemetry exports
// (both boats, all 4 events: Lanzarote, Sardinia, Marstrand, Cowes), bypassing
// the Njord raw-telemetry CDN entirely. Each phase is a true 10-second segment
// at 1Hz resolution, requiring mean BSP% (Polar Performance %) between 70% and
// 130% and a TWA range <= 6 deg across the window. Point-of-sail (upwind/downwind)
// is classified per-second from TWA: |TWA| > 100deg = downwind, |TWA| < 75deg =
// upwind, 75-100deg excluded (transition). Phases below 5kt true wind speed are
// excluded (too few/noisy samples).
//
// The 130% Polar Performance % cap matters: without it, the "top 20% by boat
// speed" selection below was systematically picking phases where the TWS sensor
// under-read (inflating BSP% well past 200% in some cases), not genuinely fast
// sailing -- producing unrealistic target speeds. Capping first removes ~13-15%
// of phases as likely sensor noise before targets are computed.
//
// Targets per TWS bin are the AVERAGE of the top ~20% of phases by boat speed in
// that bin (minimum 3 phases), from the cleaned phase set -- not a single best
// phase. TWA/AWA/Heel/Rudder/TrimTab are averaged as absolute values so port and
// starboard tacks do not cancel out; Forestay load is unsigned already. VMG% is
// the H5000's own Polar Performance % column.
//
// targetsByBoat/statsByBoat are precomputed separately for all/gemera/artemis so the
// boat filter on the page recomputes accurate top-20%-per-bin targets rather than just
// hiding points from a combined-boat target line.
//
// points: [boatCode(0=Gemera,1=Artemis), tws, bsp, twa, heel, awa, rudder, trimtab, forestay, vmgPct]
